# Build context is app/ — Docker ignores files matching patterns relative to
# this dir. The repo-root .dockerignore is NOT automatically used when context=app/.
# (CI build job: docker build -t ... -f app/<svc>/Dockerfile app/)
#
# Principle recap from AGENTS.md: build context is ALWAYS app/, per-service
# Dockerfiles COPY shared/ and pip install ./shared from sibling dir at build root.

# Exclude VCS + tooling caches
**/.git
**/.github
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info/**

# Dead per-service copies (AGENTS.md §"Stale dead code" — do not ship stale files
# that violate the fail-closed secrets contract). Services import from shared.*.
**/*-service/vault_client.py

# Reports / findings / generated artifacts
**/findings.md
**/*.md
